Frontend is the visible, interactive part of a website or application that users interact with directly in their web browser. It is built using core web technologies like HTML for structure, CSS for styling, and JavaScript for functionality and responsiveness. Ultimately, its main goal is to provide a seamless, accessible, and user-friendly experience by properly presenting data delivered from the backend.
If you are interested, I can:
• Explain the difference between frontend and backend
• Recommend the best tools and frameworks for beginners (like React or Vue)
• Share the basic skills needed to become a frontend developer
Let me know how you would like to explore this topic!

what is frontend in 3 sentence.

Frontend is the user-facing part of a website or application that you see and interact with directly in your browser. It translates complex code into visual elements using three core languages: HTML for structure, CSS for design, and JavaScript for interactivity. Its main purpose is to create a responsive, efficient, and visually appealing experience across all devices.
If you want to dive deeper, let me know if you would like to:
• Explore the top frontend frameworks like React or Vue
• Compare the differences between frontend and backend
• See a simple code example of how HTML, CSS, and JS work together


